":"### Describe the bug\n\nWhen running a triton kernel with `TRITON_INTERPRETER=1`, `tl.load` return invalid values.\r\nIt can be reproduced by taking the first add tutorial `01-vector-add.py` and adding `pdb.set_trace()` after `x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask)`. Then once in pdb, displaying x shows garbage values:\r\n```\r\n(Pdb) x\r\narray([4.6e-44, 4.6e-44, 4.6e-44, ..., 4.6e-44, 4.6e-44, 4.6e-44],\r\n    dtype=float32)\r\n```\r\nSee the [full gist ](https://gist.github.com/TheoBoyer/9f146b672c98fda65add387f9e95851a)for the total code.\r\n\r\nI tried investigating, it seems initially that the ptr was in fact a GPU addresses and intepreter as I understand it is running on CPU, so I tried to call the kernel with tensors living on CPU memory.\r\nTracking down the code execution ultimately lead to [`triton/runtime/interpreter.py:376`](https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/blob/73ba8b639226fbc505115db59189a1362c350075/python/triton/runtime/interpreter.py#L380). When calling `_interpreter.load` the addresses seem correct, as running `ctypes.cast(ptrs.data[i].item(), ctypes.POINTER(ctypes.c_float)).contents.value` return the correct value.\r\nHowever `_interpreter.load` returned an array full of `-5.886960226273074e-38`.\n\n### Environment details\n\nTriton: '3.0.0'\r\nGPU: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop GPU","closed_at":"2024-12-10T14:13:40Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38444438?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheoBoyer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheoBoyer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheoBoyer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheoBoyer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TheoBoyer","id":38444438,"login":"TheoBoyer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NDQ0NDM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheoBoyer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheoBoyer/received